# TypeScript

Strict TypeScript. Prefer small modules with named exports.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
function paint(ctx: any, tool: any) {}

// ✅ GOOD
export function paintSegment(ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D, segment: Segment): void {}
```

- No `any` unless a library ships without types; narrow it at the boundary.
- Keep drawing state in `src/state.ts`. Pass `now` into animation sampling so GIF export can render frames without the wall clock.
- Pixel tools (fill, filters, black hole) operate on the 960×640 backing store, not CSS pixels.
